│ To resolve the issue of overriding get_FIELD_display() in Django   │
│ 2.2+, we need to understand the behavior of Django's model display │
│ logic and how it interacts with the __str__ method.                │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                           ✅ Root Cause                            │
│                                                                    │
│ In Django 2.2+, the get_FIELD_display() method is not available in │
│ the context of the model's __str__ method. Instead, the field's    │
│ display() method is used to return the appropriate value. This     │
│ change in behavior is not documented in the Django changelog, and  │
│ it is not supported in Django 2.2+.                                │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                             🛠️ Solution                             │
│                                                                    │
│ The correct approach is to use the field's display() method        │
│ instead of overriding get_FIELD_display(). This is the correct way │
│ to override the display logic for a specific field in Django.      │
│                                                                    │
│                              Example:                              │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  class FooBar(models.Model):                                       │
│      foo_bar = models.CharField(_("foo"), choices=[(1, 'foo'), (2  │
│  'bar')])                                                          │
│                                                                    │
│      def __str__(self):                                            │
│          return self.foo_bar.display()                             │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                 🔍 Why the Original Approach Fails                 │
│                                                                    │
│  • In Django 2.2+, the __str__ method of the model calls the       │
│    display() method of the field, not get_FIELD_display().         │
│  • Overriding get_FIELD_display() is not a valid approach in this  │
│    context.                                                        │
│  • The get_FIELD_display() method is not part of the model's       │
│    __str__ logic in Django 2.2+.                                   │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
