╭─ Context Retrieval Agent (Model response (context analysis)) ──────╮
│                       🔍 Analysis of Context                       │
│                                                                    │
│ The root cause of the issue is that in Django 2.2+, the __str__    │
│ method of a model does not call get_FIELD_DISPLAY(). Instead, it   │
│ calls the display() method of the field. This is a breaking change │
│ that is not documented in the Django changelog, and it is not      │
│ supported in Django 2.2+.                                          │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│               🛠️ Bug Locations and Intended Behavior                │
│                                                                    │
│ Location 1:                                                        │
│                                                                    │
│  • File: foo_bar/models.py                                         │
│  • Class: FooBar                                                   │
│  • Method: __str__                                                 │
│  • Intended Behavior:                                              │
│    Replace get_foo_bar_display() with self.foo_bar.display() to    │
│    align with Django 2.2+ behavior. This ensures the __str__       │
│    method returns the correct field value (e.g., 'foo' or 'bar')   │
│    as expected.                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ Location 2:                                                        │
│                                                                    │
│  • File: models.py                                                 │
│  • Class: FooBar                                                   │
│  • Method: get_foo_bar_display                                     │
│  • Intended Behavior:                                              │
│    Remove this method since it is not used in Django 2.2+ and is   │
│    redundant. The __str__ method already calls display() on the    │
│    field, so this method is obsolete.                              │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                             ✅ Summary                             │
│                                                                    │
│ The bug is in the __str__ method of FooBar, which should call      │
│ display() instead of get_FIELD_DISPLAY. The get_foo_bar_display    │
│ method is obsolete and should be removed. The class FooBar is      │
│ defined in foo_bar/models.py, but its exact location is not        │
│ determined due to the lack of context. The intended behavior is to │
│ use display() for field display in Django 2.2+.                    │
